{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774201787,"nonce":"ZYPNk+XzRXZyfgcfVwBTu6f4LT8=","message":"Design decision: disallowedTools + MCP tool is the correct approach\n\nVerified that disallowedTools works in YOLO mode (bypassPermissions). The SDK docs confirm deny rules are evaluated before the permission mode: \"Deny rules are checked first and hold in every permission mode, including bypassPermissions.\"\n\nImplementation plan:\n- SDKBackend passes disallowedTools: [\"Agent\"] in query options\n- mandible_spawn_agent MCP tool serves as the only delegation mechanism\n- No need for stub agents or agents parameter gymnastics\n\nImportant caveat: allowedTools does NOT constrain YOLO mode (it only pre-approves; unlisted tools fall through to bypassPermissions which auto-approves everything). Only disallowedTools provides hard exclusion.\n\nThe preset/system prompt for Mandible-spawned sessions must include a convention telling the agent to use mandible_spawn_agent for all subagent delegation, and explaining that the Agent tool is unavailable. This belongs in the preset rather than CLAUDE.md since it only applies to Mandible-spawned sessions (not channel or external sessions where the Agent tool works normally).","files":null}]}